      "message": "FYI we recently merged into 16-6.12/arm64/pkvm the use of MMU notifiers for non-protected VMs. This lets us hook events like page ageing and swapping so that Hyp can update second-level page tables. This means we no longer pin non-protected pages, and also memory ballooning/reclaim can work with no patches needed on the guest side to force unpin. Of course these advantages are for non-p VMs only.",
